&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an AI Research Intern to join our founding team and bridge the gap between high-level AI research and real-world physical actuation for our next-generation autonomous transport platforms. In this role, you will contribute to core research initiatives on Perception, World Models and Action models. You will help translate cutting-edge theoretical breakthroughs into scalable, real-world deployment on physical autonomous systems, driving how our platforms perceive, simulate, and navigate complex environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate and adapt emerging AI research into internal model pipelines, validating performance on real-world datasets and simulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype and evaluate RL, trajectory planning, and distillation algorithms based on state-of-the-art literature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and fine-tune multimodal models that map real-time sensor inputs and behavioral goals to vehicle actuation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment with world model architectures using multi-sensor log data to improve simulation fidelity and trajectory querying.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze edge cases and failure modes in novel driving environments to iterate on model performance and stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run rigorous simulation experiments alongside research and validation teams to identify performance bottlenecks and track model improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently enrolled in a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree program in Computer Science, EECS, Robotics, AI, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Coursework, project experience, or research background focused on at least one of the following domains:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generative World Models / Video Generation / Diffusion Models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models or embodied AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforcement Learning (RL), trajectory optimization, or decision-making systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large-scale multimodal Transformer architectures applied to robotics or spatio-temporal data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Framework Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced hands-on proficiency with PyTorch or JAX for training and fine-tuning large-scale neural networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in Python and working knowledge of C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior research, project, or internship experience in autonomous driving, mobile robotics, or spatial AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
