&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Namaa, we build and operate tech-enabled urban infrastructure that gives consumers fast, reliable access to meals, groceries, and everyday essentials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Traditional retail models, built around brick-and-mortar locations, often struggle to compete in today’s digital-first landscape. Challenges such as cost efficiency per square foot, logistics-optimized locations, and seamless technology integration have made it clear that a new approach is needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the future of foodservice and commerce lies in purpose-built infrastructure designed for speed, accuracy, and scalability. That’s why Namaa was established—to power the next generation of digital food and quick commerce ecosystems across the Middle East.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ecosystem is driven by a portfolio of specialized business units, including &lt;strong&gt;KitchenPark&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;CloudRetail&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Profood Properties&lt;/strong&gt;, each playing a key role in enabling brands to grow and thrive in an increasingly on-demand world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re looking for an experienced procurement and contracts professional with a strong background in construction, real estate, or facilities management, and hands-on experience in sourcing, commercial negotiations, cost control, and vendor contracts.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Procurement:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead complete sourcing cycles, RFP developments, technical/commercial evaluations, and vendor selections across company projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Strategy &amp;amp; Budget Protection:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct detailed market price assessments, unit-rate benchmarks, and BOQ analyses to mitigate cost inflation and keep projects under budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract Negotiations &amp;amp; Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Draft, negotiate, and finalize commercial agreements, Master Service Agreements (MSAs), SLAs, Purchase Orders and Variation Orders with suppliers and subcontractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Risk Mitigation:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure strict compliance with internal procurement workflows, financial approval limits, and contractual risk controls to eliminate corporate liability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Relationship &amp;amp; Performance Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Retain high-performing suppliers, audit ongoing vendor delivery against agreed SLAs, and lead commercial dispute resolutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the strategic bridge between Construction, Operations, Legal, and Finance teams to translate operational requirements into enforceable commercial terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3-5+ years of progressive experience in commercial procurement, strategic sourcing, or contract management (construction, real estate, or FM experience preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contractual Mastery&lt;/strong&gt;: knowledge in drafting, reviewing, and negotiating commercial contracts, risk allocation, and legal terms with external suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Acumen&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong proficiency in cost modeling, unit-rate benchmarking, invoice auditing, and analyzing market-wide material price trends.&lt;/li&gt;
