&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atoms is building the machines that power the next era of progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the last decade, software has transformed the digital world. But the physical world, where food is made, minerals are mined, goods are moved, and industries are run, remains far less intelligent, far less efficient, and far more constrained. We’re changing that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atoms builds Physical AI— real-world robots for the industries that move civilization forward, starting with food, mining, and transport. Our systems are designed to understand, predict, and control the real world with precision, turning complex physical operations into something more reliable, more scalable, and more productive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This work requires more than robotics. It requires deep integration across hardware, software, AI, operations, manufacturing, and real estate. We don’t just build machines in a lab. We deploy them into real environments, operate them, learn from them, and improve them until they work at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are roboticists, engineers, operators, and builders. We believe the next great technology companies will not only transform information, but the physical systems that shape everyday life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to work on hard problems with real-world impact, join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Civil Engineer to support the evaluation, design, permitting, and execution of facility development projects across our growing portfolio. As part of our vertically integrated engineering team, you will be responsible for assessing site feasibility, utility infrastructure, drainage systems, grading, ADA compliance, and external utility coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is highly focused on existing-site evaluation and infrastructure strategy. We are looking for engineers who can quickly assess site constraints, understand utility availability and capacity, and develop practical, cost-effective solutions that support project schedules and operational requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Architecture, Structural, Mechanical, Plumbing, Geotechnical, Construction, Development, and Operations teams to ensure sites are designed for constructability, regulatory compliance, and long-term operational success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform site due diligence assessments for prospective and active development projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate local permitting requirements, utility regulations, development standards, and jurisdictional requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate existing utility infrastructure, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domestic water&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fire water&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sanitary sewer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Storm drainage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural gas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical service infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with utility providers to determine service availability, capacities, connection requirements, and upgrade needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop utility connection strategies from public infrastructure to building connection points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and coordinate:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Site utility systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grading and drainage plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stormwater management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grease interceptor locations and site integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paving improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curb and gutter systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ADA access routes and site accessibility improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop stormwater management strategies, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SWPPP requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low Impact Development (LID) measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stormwater Best Management Practices (BMPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Water quality requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Architectural and Plumbing teams to determine optimal locations for:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grease interceptors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utility entry points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fire water services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical service equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Water and gas connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with surveyors and geotechnical consultants to evaluate site conditions, access constraints, environmental concerns, and constructability challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce schematic designs, permit drawings, and construction documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support entitlement, permitting, bid review, and construction administration activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Authorities Having Jurisdiction (AHJs), utility agencies, and public works departments throughout project development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support value engineering efforts and identify opportunities to simplify site construction, reduce costs, and accelerate schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Focus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
