&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating a large, owned fleet means a steady flow of auto and general liability&amp;nbsp;claims—and a steady flow of correspondence from carriers, adjusters, and attorneys.&amp;nbsp;As Claims Administrator/Coordinator, you are the responsive front line of claims&amp;nbsp;operation: reporting new claims quickly, keeping every file moving, and making sure&amp;nbsp;nothing (a demand, a subpoena, a document request) falls through the cracks. You free&amp;nbsp;up our Claims Manager to focus on strategy and severity while you own intake and&amp;nbsp;day-to-day coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle first notice of loss (FNOL): intake new claims and report them promptly and accurately to carriers/TPAs—speed here directly reduces claim cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the claims inbox: acknowledge, triage, and respond to correspondence from adjusters, defense counsel, plaintiff attorneys, and third-party carriers within defined SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and distribute claim documentation—police reports, Samsara telematics and dashcam footage, driver statements, trip and vehicle records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log and route time-sensitive items (demand letters, subpoenas, litigation notices) and escalate per protocol.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, current claims log / RMIS and track status, deadlines, and open items across all files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce regular claim status and open-inventory reports for the Claims Manager and Risk leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process certificate-of-insurance and coverage-confirmation requests tied to active claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
