&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Robotics, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Technical Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid foundation in circuit design, analog/digital fundamentals, and basic embedded systems logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with PCB design tools (e.g., Altium, KiCad, Eagle) and bench equipment (oscilloscopes, multimeters, logic analyzers) through lab work, student design teams (e.g., Formula SAE, Robotics Club), or personal projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protocols &amp;amp; Hardware:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity or coursework covering common hardware communication protocols (CAN, SPI, I2C, UART).&lt;/li&gt;
