&lt;p&gt;If you want to work on hard problems with real-world impact, join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead electrical system design and analysis — power distribution, service entrance design, panel/switchgear sizing, lighting, and emergency/standby power — for new and retrofit facilities across Atoms&#39; portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare electrical calculations, drawings, and specifications for permit submittal across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design power distribution and charging circuits for EV/AV charging and support infrastructure, including coordinating transformer and service upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with utility providers to secure power availability, service upgrades, and timely energization for new sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Structural, Building Design, Civil, and MEP consultant teams to resolve system conflicts and keep designs constructible and cost-effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and respond to plan check comments from Authorities Having Jurisdiction (AHJs) and utility providers to keep permitting and energization on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate vendor and manufacturer electrical equipment submittals (switchgear, EV charging hardware, backup power systems) for code compliance and site suitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction administration, including RFIs, submittal review, and field observation for electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and refine standardized electrical details and design templates that can be reused across Atoms&#39; different business lines to support rapid, repeatable deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10 years of electrical engineering experience, including design for commercial, industrial, or high-power facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) license preferred; ability to obtain additional state licensure/reciprocity as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with power distribution, service entrance, and panel/switchgear design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NEC, NFPA 70/70E, and local utility interconnection requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing permit-ready electrical drawings and independently managing AHJ and utility plan review/energization cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Atoms, you’ll work on one of the defining challenges of our time—bringing automation into the physical world to drive real, lasting impact. We exist to uncover valuable unknown truths and turn them into progress, which means constantly pushing beyond what’s known and building what doesn’t yet exist. The work is ambitious and often challenging, but it’s grounded in a shared sense of purpose and a team committed to seeing it through together. Our work only matters if it serves others, and we know that meaningful progress depends on the trust of the people we serve and the strength of our team—so we invest in both, creating an environment where you can do your best work and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What else you need to know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our San Francisco office. Atoms is a company driven by invention and continuous change - we are constantly reimagining our industries, building new products, and refining how we operate. We do our best work together. That’s why all of our office-based teams work onsite, five days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
