&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Field Service Technician is a hands-on role responsible for the installation, preventive maintenance, and repair of Pronto&#39;s autonomous haulage technology across a range of customer mine sites. This position plays a critical role in ensuring successful deployment and optimal performance of Pronto equipment in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Installation &amp;amp; Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;: Installs, commissions, and troubleshoots autonomous retrofit kits on heavy-duty mining equipment at active open-pit sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works on customer sites as part of a deployment crew, often as the sole technical presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preventive Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;: Carry out scheduled maintenance tasks to ensure system health, reliability, and long-term performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and log equipment conditions, identifying signs of wear, degradation, or environmental impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Troubleshooting &amp;amp; Repair&lt;/strong&gt;: Diagnose and repair hardware, software, and connectivity issues in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Serve as the face of Pronto during on-site visits, maintaining professional and responsive communication with customer personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years hands-on experience as a heavy equipment, diesel, automotive technician, avionics, industrial controls, or military/vehicle maintenance technician&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on low-voltage (12/24V DC) electrical work: harness routing, connector termination, crimping, sensor and actuator installation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read and work from wiring diagrams, schematics, and installation drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to mobilize on short notice (24 - 72 hours) and deploy for multi-week rotations, role is ~75% travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid US drivers license&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with site conditions: extreme heat/cold, dust, altitude, shift work including nights and weekends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with standard business tools (email, ticketing systems, spreadsheets, documentation platforms, instant messaging, and typical suite platforms)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Makes sound judgment calls independently on site, with limited real-time support and often poor connectivity, and represent the company professionally at customer sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator internally and externally with internal engineering as well as mine site crews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on real, production-deployed autonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technology that directly improves safety, efficiency, and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex challenges in demanding, real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a fast-moving team with high ownership and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See your work deployed and making a difference in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with experienced engineers and industry operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
