&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Inventory Specialist, you will own inventory accuracy and the system of record across our production facilities. While the warehouse team moves material, you make sure the data matches reality: you design and maintain the bin location system, run the cycle count program, reconcile every discrepancy, and control access to high-value stock. In an operation scaling toward 1,000 vehicles, your work is what keeps the build plan trustworthy and prevents stock-outs before they stop the line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the inventory system of record; hold sole authority for inventory adjustments and reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain bin locations across facilities so every part has a defined home&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and perform the cycle count program end to end: schedule counts, count physically, analyze results, and drive root-cause on repeat misses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile discrepancies surfaced at receiving, picking, kitting, and counting; document findings and corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the stock cage: control access, track issuance, and maintain accountability for high-value components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain min/max thresholds per part; flag stock-outs and shortage risks to the Buyer and Supply Chain Manager before they hit the build plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain serialized traceability records (PO to serial to VIN) and support audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report inventory accuracy metrics weekly and drive continuous improvement in count accuracy and record discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support inventory setup for new production sites as they come online&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in inventory control, inventory analysis, or warehouse operations with direct cycle count responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data discipline: comfortable working in inventory/ERP systems and spreadsheets daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to investigate and reconcile inventory discrepancies to root cause&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and commitment to accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while coordinating with warehouse, purchasing, and production teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing bin location systems, cycle count programs, or inventory controls from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP/MRP or WMS systems in a manufacturing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with serialized or lot-controlled inventory and traceability requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in manufacturing, automotive, robotics, or technology hardware environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
