&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manufacturing/Sub Assembly Technician, you will build the sensor pods and sub-assemblies that go onto our autonomous vehicles. Working from engineering drawings and work instructions, you&#39;ll assemble brackets, sensors, and harnessing into finished sensor pods, and make sure every fastener is torqued to spec, and every pod is solid before it moves to vehicle installation. This is an entry-level role: senior technicians and leads will train you on our build process, tools, and quality standards. You&#39;ll work in a fast-moving production environment where processes and designs are actively evolving, so precision matters and so does speaking up when something doesn&#39;t look right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assemble sensor pods from components, including mounting and aligning sensors, brackets, and enclosures per engineering drawings and work instructions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and stage sub-assemblies (brackets, mounts, harness segments, and hardware kits) ahead of final pod and vehicle install&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Torque all fasteners to spec using calibrated torque tools, and mark/verify torque (e.g., torque striping) so every pod is secure and vibration-ready&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Route and secure pod wiring with proper connector seating, strain relief, and cable management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality checks on finished pods and sub-assemblies (fit, fastener security, connector checks) before handoff to installation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow standard operating procedures and flag gaps, unclear steps, missing or wrong parts, and design issues to leads and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log build issues in the issue tracker so engineering can close the loop on part and design problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately document completed builds, serial numbers, and checks as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support rework when design updates roll out to existing pods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete on-the-job training and build proficiency across assembly stations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, organized, and safe work area, including tool and part organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
