&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pronto AI is a global leader in commercializing autonomous vehicle (AV) technology, deploying Autonomous Haulage Systems (AHS) that automate operations in mines, quarries, and construction sites worldwide. While much of the industry remains in R&amp;amp;D, we deliver real, production-ready autonomy that is already operating in the field. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are on a mission to make mining operations safer, smarter, and more efficient through cutting-edge technology, and we are building toward becoming the world’s first profitable AV technology company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery &amp;amp; Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success Criteria:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver projects to the agreed-upon performance metrics and success criteria, ensuring the autonomous system is integrated seamlessly into the mine’s production cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the local field team, overseeing permitting, scheduling, safety compliance, and overall work performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Hold the customer accountable for their deliverables, including resource commitments, machine availability, and site/route/equipment readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Liaison&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Point of Contact:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the central communication hub between the customer site and Pronto HQ, providing regular progress reports and escalating technical or operational blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with customers to set up or modify existing operational processes to accommodate autonomous haulage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Handover &amp;amp; Training:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the customer training programs on Pronto technology and manage the formal handover of the system to the mine’s operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mining Expertise: 15+ years of direct mining experience. You must be extremely comfortable and knowledgeable in a mine site environment, understanding the nuances of production and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership Tenure: 5–10 years in a leadership role (e.g., Site Superintendent, Maintenance Manager, or Fleet Manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech Rollout Experience: Proven track record of actively participating in technology rollouts, such as autonomy, remote operations, telematics, or machine control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: A University Degree in Mining Engineering is highly preferred to establish immediate credibility with customer stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Must be based in AZ, CA, TX or WY.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Authority: The ability to command respect on-site and influence customer decision-making to ensure site readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability: Deep understanding of how to transition a mine from manual to technology-assisted or autonomous operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills for reporting to executive-level stakeholders at both the customer and Pronto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions &amp;amp; Schedule&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Site Deployment: &lt;/strong&gt;This is an on-site role. During deployments, you will stay regional to the customer in local accommodations or in customer-provided quarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mining Schedule: &lt;/strong&gt;Working schedules are based on mining rotations (e.g., x weeks on, y weeks off) rather than a standard office week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current Project Commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; To complete the existing demo at Ma’aden, the successful candidate should expect to spend approximately 2 months remaining on-site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on real, production-deployed autonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technology that directly improves safety, efficiency, and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex challenges in demanding, real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a fast-moving team with high ownership and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See your work deployed and making a difference in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with experienced engineers and industry operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What else you need to know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a field-based role supporting operations across the United States and international locations. Atoms is a company driven by invention and continuous change—we are constantly reimagining our industries, building new products, and refining how we operate. This position requires travel across up to 75% of the time. Candidates should be comfortable with frequent travel and a highly mobile work environment.&lt;/p&gt;
