&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant experience as an in-house paralegal, legal assistant or within a law firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with corporate/company secretarial matters, entity management and corporate documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Middle East jurisdictions and an understanding of local corporate and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Arabic and English&lt;/strong&gt;, written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational and time-management skills, with excellent attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and comfortable taking ownership of matters from start to finish, including following up with multiple stakeholders and external providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and coordination skills, with the ability to work effectively across different teams, jurisdictions and external advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fast-paced, evolving environment and managing multiple priorities and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A practical, solutions-oriented approach and the ability to identify issues, follow up independently and keep matters moving.&lt;/li&gt;
