&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the past, to be a successful restaurateur, you simply had to have a passion for food and a passion for people - but to succeed as a digital restaurateur you also need to have a passion for technology. We believe in the joy of serving others, and that&#39;s why we created Otter – to help restaurateurs succeed in online food delivery. Restaurants around the world, both large and small, including Chick-fil-A, Ben &amp;amp; Jerry’s, KFC, and Eataly trust our software to power their delivery business. We increase sales, reduce order issues, and decrease delivery headaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a high-leverage team building Otter’s Guest Engagement products – the suite of tools that help restaurants drive demand, turn customers into loyal repeat fans across millions of eater interactions. You’ll own end-to-end product outcomes from strategy through execution and iteration in a portfolio that also includes discounting, loyalty programs, eater personalization, and marketing. Our customers’ success is your success. You will help define how Otter’s global Guest Engagement strategy evolves, not just how it is executed. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate restaurant growth goals into products that increase acquisition, conversion, frequency, and lifetime value and prioritize the highest-leverage opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the core platform capabilities behind promotions, loyalty, offers, and personalization across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for measurable impact: run experiments, define holdouts, and quantify incremental revenue and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help restaurants reach the right eater with the right message at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across globally, setting direction and driving alignment through clear product narratives, documentation, and reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes, not just launches: move metrics like redemption, repeat rate, retention, ROI, and campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate strategy, progress, and results to global stakeholders through well-crafted written and verbal updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new opportunities, shape the roadmap, and influence investment decisions for your product area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience (or equivalent) in growth, marketing technology, loyalty, promotions, or personalization products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of shipping products that drove measurable impact on acquisition, conversion, retention, or lifetime value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experimentation mindset: comfortable defining hypotheses, success metrics, holdouts, and reading incrementality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluent: you can run your own analysis or work with analysts and data scientists to build segments, targeting logic, and performance measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent product judgment &amp;amp; UX instincts — you can simplify complex marketing capabilities into tools operators can actually use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can influence cross-functional partners and senior stakeholders in a global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High bar for written product thinking (PRDs, strategy docs, experiment readouts).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable representing your product area in global reviews and leadership forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM, marketing automation, offers, or loyalty systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with omni-channel commerce and customer identity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building tools that balance merchant control with automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in restaurants, retail, or local commerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Massive opportunity: Restaurants are still early in adopting the tools that modern digital businesses rely on. You’ll help define how the next generation of growth infrastructure gets built. In the last 5 years, just in the US, the overall market has expanded 10X from $10B to $100B, and could expand to $500bn- $1T by 2030.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will ship products that thousands of operators depend on every day to drive revenue.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership, high visibility, and real influence on strategy in a company defining a new category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What else you need to know&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Beijing office location. As a company driven by innovation and continuous change, close collaboration is essential. We’re constantly reimagining our industry, creating new products, and refining our processes, and we do our best work together. That’s why all of our office-based teams work onsite, five days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to join us as we serve those who serve others?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;#LI-Onsite&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atoms is building the machines that power the next era of progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the last decade, software has transformed the digital world. But the physical world, where food is made, minerals are mined, goods are moved, and industries are run, remains far less intelligent, far less efficient, and far more constrained. We’re changing that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atoms builds Physical AI real-world robots for the industries that move civilization forward, starting with food, mining, and transport. Our systems are designed to understand, predict, and control the real world with precision, turning complex physical operations into something more reliable, more scalable, and more productive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Atoms, Otter is building the digital infrastructure for better food. Restaurants today face a world where off-premise demand is growing faster than the tools built to support it. We help operators simplify complexity, grow their business, and deliver great experiences to every guest – wherever they are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform empowers food businesses of all sizes, from local heroes to regional chains and global enterprises. With Otter, restaurants can focus on what they do best: serving delicious food to their customers. And as they thrive, we’re helping make better food more accessible, reliable, and affordable for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are roboticists, engineers, operators, and builders. We believe the next great technology companies will not only transform information, but the physical systems that shape everyday life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to work on hard problems with real-world impact, join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Product Manager for Otter&#39;s Integrations &amp;amp; Ecosystem domain, you&#39;ll own the connectivity engine behind every third-party integration in the Otter ecosystem - A system that links Otter to dozens of partner platforms and keeps those links authenticated, alive, and reliable at scale. You will&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define a healthy ecosystem:&lt;/strong&gt; Set the metrics that actually matter - usage, attach rate, retention lift, connections health etc and build the reporting and instrumentation that tracks ecosystem health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own connectivity engine roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and drive the technical roadmap for a single self-healing integration engine that sits behind one reliable interface for every third-party connection including credential creation and management, session persistence, health monitoring, automated recovery and beyond&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep connections alive:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Partner with engineering to design systems that survive partner-side auth changes, session expiry etc. before they cause failures using adaptive retry, rotation strategies etc that hold success rates high&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Auto-heal broken links:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the detect-and-recover loop for when connections do break. Define what &quot;broken&quot; means per integration, instrument the signals that catch failures early, and build the flows that re-establish connections automatically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale the partner surface:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Onboard new partner platforms - POS, delivery, payments, inventory, and beyond into the engine. Define the integration contract, the connection patterns each partner needs (OAuth/SSO, credential-based, webhook etc), and the certification bar every connection clears before going LIVE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Engineering, Security, Design, BD, and GTM to balance new partner coverage against the reliability, compliance, and legal posture of a system that manages credentials and maintains connections at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10 years of product management experience, with direct ownership of a technical platform, developer product, or integrations/connectivity system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in integration architecture - OAuth/SSO, credential management, session and token lifecycle, webhook design, and bidirectional data sync etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning system reliability at scale including defining SLOs, instrumenting health, and driving mean-time-to-recovery down through automated healing rather than manual ops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives across Product, Engineering, Security, Design, and BD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in restaurants, retail, or a comparably complex vertical is a meaningful advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
