&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we’re reinventing the way employees experience lunch at work. By partnering with top local restaurants and batching hundreds of orders, we make it easy for companies to offer high-quality, individually packed meals, without fees or tips. Our mission is to create a seamless, affordable, and joyful lunch experience that benefits both employees and employers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone to design and build the operational foundation that supports this growth: a territory model, industry classification, commission instrumentation, and a prospecting universe that stays aligned with our CRM as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role and the first dedicated Sales Operations hire at Picnic. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to shape the operational backbone of our commercial organization from the ground up, with a clear path to building and leading a team as it scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the reporting layer end to end&lt;/strong&gt;: define, build, and maintain the pipelines behind pipeline, forecast, conversion, productivity, and territory performance metrics, replacing ad hoc analysis with self-serve, consistent reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and implement the regional territory model in Salesforce as an enforceable system,&lt;/strong&gt; including assignment and routing rules, and own ongoing rebalancing as the team and map evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and run Book of Business processes&lt;/strong&gt;: account ownership, transitions when reps join or leave, and rules of engagement between national and local accounts, turning a manual, high-risk exercise into a routine one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the prospecting universe&lt;/strong&gt;: what data goes in, how it&#39;s enriched and scraped from external sources, how it reconciles with the CRM, and how sellers get a usable, targeted list every week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and run commissions and quota&lt;/strong&gt;: build the plans with commercial leadership, own the calculation logic, and ensure every commission statement is accurate the first time and every time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Salesforce as the system of record:&lt;/strong&gt; object model, validation rules, automation, and data quality, deciding what&#39;s worth enforcing to keep our commercial data accurate and reliable as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, daily SQL skills, you can model data, debug someone else&#39;s query, and diagnose why a number is wrong before you know what it should be.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Salesforce expertise as a system, not just a UI: object model, record types, validation rules, assignment/matching rules, flows, and clear judgment on when automation is the wrong answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building sales operations from a low base at a fast-growing company, including designing (not just maintaining) a territory model and running a full commission cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort owning the numbers you produce — able to show the derivation of any figure, and equally comfortable saying &quot;I don&#39;t know&quot; when that&#39;s the honest answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with ambiguity that won&#39;t resolve on its own — much of this role is deciding on the right definition, documenting it, and driving company-wide adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a warehouse-first analytics stack rather than reporting solely inside the CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in data enrichment, web scraping, or third-party data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in field sales, restaurant, logistics, or marketplace operations, where physical delivery makes data messier than typical SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as the first operations hire at a company, and a clear understanding of what that role demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive real impact: Be part of building the operational engine behind a fast-growing startup that’s redefining how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your city: Take full ownership of your city’s performance and see the direct results of your ideas and execution every single day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with purpose: Join a mission-driven team focused on making the workplace experience better for thousands of people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow with us&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; At Picnic, there’s room to grow—personally and professionally—as we scale and take on new challenges together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
