&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Otter POS, we build the backend that keeps restaurant point-of-sale running: orders, payments, menus, and device state across Android tablets in the kitchen and at the counter. Those services have to stay consistent when WiFi drops mid-service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a backend engineer on this team, you will design and scale the services behind order orchestration, payment flows, offline-first sync, and multi-device coordination. We want product-minded or systems-focused backend engineers. You do not need prior POS experience. If you like distributed systems, careful API design, and reliability work under real restaurant conditions, you will fit here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain Java backend services for order lifecycle, payments, device sync, and restaurant workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and optimize APIs and event-driven systems so POS devices, kitchen displays, and cloud services stay consistent with low latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build systems that keep working offline and sync across multiple devices in a facility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Android engineers, product managers, and other teams to ship systems used in live restaurants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep code quality high through testing, code reviews, observability, and owning what you ship in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
