&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring-up and commissioning engineering.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the build instructions, drawings, procedures, and commissioning gates that installations run against. Act as the engineering escalation point for field teams and convert escalations into documented design and process changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Off-machine validation.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and own the bench and simulation capability that allows releases to be validated against real truck interfaces. Own the correlation between bench behavior and truck behavior, including where the two diverge.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability, diagnostics, and fleet measurement.&lt;/strong&gt; Own availability, utilization, and subsystem failure-rate measurement, including fault attribution. Set diagnostics requirements for new hardware, and run root-cause and corrective-action discipline on field failures.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
