&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience in vehicle integration, automotive or EV service, electromechanical assembly, or fabrication.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently and troubleshoot from first principles in unstructured engineering environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging cross-disciplinary systems (mechanical, electrical, and software) at a systems-integration level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read wiring diagrams, schematics, mechanical drawings, and BOMs, and to flag a discrepancy rather than build around it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of vehicle electrical systems, including low-voltage power distribution, fusing, grounding, connectors, and CAN bus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with hand, shop, and automotive tools, and with a multimeter, oscilloscope, and soldering iron.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing procedures or documentation that others work from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle many simultaneous projects and tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to safely lift up to 50lbs and stand for long periods of time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with autonomous vehicles, EV, motorsport, aerospace, or heavy equipment is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-voltage safety training for EV work is a plus Experience with CAN tooling, vehicle bus analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
