&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Hardware Reliability Engineer to own vehicle-level reliability testing and hardware issue resolution for our on-road program. In this role, you will run a dedicated test fleet, plan and execute the durability and environmental testing behind it, and own the highest-priority vehicle hardware issues from first report through root cause, corrective action, and verification. This is a hands-on role based in the garage, on the road, and at test sites and labs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a dedicated test fleet: define duty cycles, routes, and mileage and hour targets, schedule vehicles and drivers with the operations team, and track exposure by vehicle and hardware revision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute durability and environmental testing, on the road and at external test labs, to reproduce field conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the highest-priority vehicle hardware issues: reproduce the failure, collect logs and returned parts, confirm the failure mode, and establish root cause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define containment actions, drive corrective actions with mechanical, electrical, firmware, and software engineering, and verify effectiveness on test vehicles and in the fleet before closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the return path for failed hardware from vehicle to bench, including tagging, teardown, functional confirmation, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize test and field findings into design change recommendations with supporting evidence, and represent them in design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report test fleet results on a fixed cadence: exposure by vehicle and hardware revision, failures by subsystem normalized to exposure, and status of open issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Mechatronics, or Automotive Engineering, or a related field. Equivalent hands-on experience will be considered in place of the degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in vehicle test, validation, durability, field quality, or reliability engineering on prototype, pre-production, or production vehicles in automotive, EV, autonomous vehicle, or commercial vehicle programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a test or durability fleet, including duty cycle definition, mileage accumulation planning, driver coordination, and configuration and test record control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of field or test failures from first report through reproduction, root cause, containment, corrective action, and verification, across multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on failure analysis of returned vehicle hardware, including teardown, functional confirmation on a vehicle or buck, and coordination of ingress, thermal, and vibration testing with labs.&lt;/li&gt;
