&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical, Mechanical, Industrial, or Manufacturing Engineering, or a related field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in manufacturing quality, NPI quality, or supplier quality on electronic or electromechanical hardware: PCBA, box build, harnesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compute, ECU, or electronics box-build quality in automotive, autonomous vehicle, robotics, or aerospace programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up quality on a new line or new product: control plans, inspection plans, and disposition process, without an established organization behind you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in PFMEA, control plans, 8D, 5-Why, and fishbone as working tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of an MRB or nonconformance disposition process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read mechanical drawings and GD&amp;amp;T, schematics, and BOMs well enough to write inspection criteria from them.&lt;/li&gt;
