&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you will be a technical leader responsible for connecting our core food infrastructure platform with the myriad of external systems used by our restaurant partners — and for raising the technical bar of the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect and Implement APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the design, deployment, and maintenance of robust, scalable, and secure API integrations, focusing on the reliable exchange of critical data (orders, menus, status updates) between our platform and systems like Point-of-Sale (POS) and ERPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Work primarily on the backend using modern development practices and one or more of our core languages: Java, Go, Kotlin, C++, C#, Scala or Rust.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Integrity and Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Own data flow across complex systems, defining best practices for querying, synchronizing, and modeling critical restaurant data at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Product Managers and external stakeholders in a global scope to define integration strategy and specifications, ensuring that every integration provides tangible business value and positive customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive and Mentor:&lt;/strong&gt; Own complex technical projects end-to-end, from architectural design through testing and full deployment, and mentor other engineers to elevate the quality and speed of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bachelor’s Degree required, &lt;/strong&gt;ideally&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;academic background in Computer Science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of professional experience as a Backend or Integration Software Engineer, ideally gained in big tech environments or similarly fast-moving organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep, proven ability to deliver production-ready code in at least one of our core backend stack languages: Java, Go, Kotlin, C++, or C#.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; A clear willingness to grow, a love for technical challenges, and a proactive, problem-solving attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated experience owning projects and solutions where you can clearly articulate and demonstrate the impact you had on technical architecture and business stakeholder problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language:&lt;/strong&gt; Good English proficiency, as you will be collaborating with our global team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Atoms, you’ll work on one of the defining challenges of our time—bringing automation into the physical world to drive real, lasting impact. We exist to uncover valuable unknown truths and turn them into progress, which means constantly pushing beyond what’s known and building what doesn’t yet exist. The work is ambitious and often challenging, but it’s grounded in a shared sense of purpose and a team committed to seeing it through together. Our work only matters if it serves others, and we know that meaningful progress depends on the trust of the people we serve and the strength of our team—so we invest in both, creating an environment where you can do your best work and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What else you need to know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our São Paulo&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;office. Atoms is a company driven by invention and continuous change - we are constantly reimagining our industries, building new products, and refining how we operate. We do our best work together. That’s why all of our office-based teams work onsite, five days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
