&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Software Engineer to build the log replay and scenario execution systems at the core of our simulation platform. In this role, you will take a recorded log from storage, to a replayable test case, to a scored result, and own the execution, determinism, and reporting in between. You will do this across on-road and off-highway programs, and you will own the tooling other engineers use to run scenario suites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log replay. Build the pipeline that converts recorded logs into replayable test cases, including ingest, indexing, retrieval, and replay of a specific run on demand. Implement open-loop scoring against ground truth and closed-loop replay where the simulated machine is allowed to diverge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scenario execution. Build the execution layer that runs a scenario identically every time, including clock control, seed and configuration management, and results traceable to a software version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous integration. Integrate simulation into CI. Maintain the commit, nightly, and regression workflows, and keep failures attributable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics and reporting. Implement the pass criteria and metrics a release is judged against, and the reporting that reduces a batch of failing runs to an actionable list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale and cost. Run large batches efficiently, track the cost of a simulation run, and reduce it as volume grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tooling. Build the interfaces, visualizations, and command-line tools that make the platform usable by engineers who did not build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional work. Work with autonomy and robotics on failure definitions, with bench and hardware-in-the-loop engineering on the path from simulation to bench to vehicle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, or a related field with 5+ years of software engineering experience, or a master&#39;s with 3+ years required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in C++ and Python, including the ability to read, navigate, and debug large codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating data or test infrastructure at scale, including pipelines, batch execution, storage and indexing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with simulation, log replay, or large-scale automated testing for robotics or autonomous vehicles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with a robotics middleware and its logging and replay tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling autonomous driving or robotics sensor data across multiple modalities and timestamps, including camera, LiDAR, and radar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of determinism and reproducibility, including clock control, seed management, and configuration pinning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating test workloads into continuous integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency with modern AI coding and agentic development tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication covering design notes and test results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel occasionally to deployment and test sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite five days a week in San Francisco.&lt;/li&gt;
