&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Vehicle Integration Engineer to own vehicle bring-up and sensor calibration across our autonomous platforms. In this role, you will take a vehicle from mechanically complete, to first autonomous engagement, to a validated unit released into the fleet, owning the sequence, the calibration method, and the acceptance criteria that determine when a vehicle is ready. You will build the calibration and test infrastructure that turns bring-up from an engineering activity into a repeatable process the production team can run without you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vehicle Bring-Up: Own the bring-up sequence end to end: power-on, firmware and software load, device enumeration, systems validation, first autonomous engagement validation and the sign-off that releases a vehicle to the fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sensor Calibration: Own intrinsic and extrinsic calibration across the full sensor suite of lidar, radar, camera, IMU, and GNSS. Build and maintain the physical calibration environment, define what &quot;in calibration&quot; means, how it is verified, and how a drifting or incorrect calibration is caught early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test Plans &amp;amp; Validation: Author the test plans and procedures our fleet is validated against, execute them, analyze the resulting data, and report results clearly enough to act on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Domain Diagnosis: Resolve ambiguous failures across the mechanical, electrical, firmware, and software boundary, and hand the owning engineer reproduction steps and evidence rather than a symptom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test Hardware &amp;amp; Tooling: Specify, build, and maintain the benches, harness breakouts, and diagnostic tooling the process depends on, building what does not yet exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design Feedback: Feed what you learn back into hardware design (e.g. sensor mounting and tolerance stack-ups that make calibration difficult).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technician Partnership: Partner with our engineering technicians as customers, who will execute the builds and bring-up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field is required, or equivalent hands-on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years integrating, validating, and debugging electrical and electromechanical systems on prototype and production vehicles in autonomous vehicles, EVs, or at an automotive OEM or supplier, with a proven track record of technical ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise in vehicle E/E architecture: low-voltage power distribution and redundancy, wire harness and connector systems for both low and high voltage, and the failure modes that come with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with automotive networks and diagnostics (CAN, CAN FD, Automotive Ethernet, and DTCs) and the supporting tooling, including Vector CANalyzer, Vehicle Spy, oscilloscopes, and logic analyzers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating and debugging vehicle actuation interfaces: steering, braking, and propulsion, or comparable motor-control and powertrain systems, including redundant, degraded, and fail-operational behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating compute into vehicles: carrier boards, high-speed differential signaling, power sequencing, and thermal management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to navigate highly ambiguous environments, self-direct technical problem-solving, and clearly communicate technical trade-offs to cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
