&lt;p&gt;This work requires more than robotics. It requires deep integration across hardware, software, AI, operations, manufacturing, and real estate. We don’t just build machines in a lab. We deploy them into real environments, operate them, learn from them, and improve them until they work at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are roboticists, engineers, operators, and builders. We believe the next great technology companies will not only transform information, but the physical systems that shape everyday life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to work on hard problems with real-world impact, join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Special Projects Director, Marketing to drive Atom’s highest-leverage growth bets — partnering with Product and Engineering on PLG and upsell motions, and leading GTM for new partnership launches. You&#39;ll operate where marketing, product, and BD intersect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Product and Engineering on product-led growth. Help shape onboarding, activation, in-product nudges, and lifecycle triggers that get restaurant operators to value faster and keep them there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Otter&#39;s upsell and cross-sell motion across the product suite (order aggregation, virtual brands, analytics, and more). Identify the highest-leverage expansion opportunities, partner with eng/product to build the surfaces and signals, and run the campaigns that drive cross-product adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive funnel and conversion improvements across the customer journey — signup, activation, and expansion. Write hypotheses, scope experiments with PMs and engineers, and read results honestly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead GTM for new partnership launches. Define positioning, target segments, launch sequencing, and success metrics. Coordinate Product, BD, Sales, Brand, and Lifecycle so each launch lands coherently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the 0-to-1 motion for each partnership launch: positioning, messaging, launch plan, sales enablement, website surfaces, lifecycle campaigns, and measurement framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a quantitative experimentation roadmap with clear hypotheses, prioritization, and a cadence that compounds learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the measurement infrastructure that gives leadership confidence in growth decisions — funnel reporting, cohort analysis, and experiment readouts using GA4, Mixpanel, Looker, or Snowflake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead other high-leverage special projects outside the standard roadmap — segment expansions, pricing/packaging changes, and anything else leadership wants pushed hard for a quarter or two.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Performance Marketing, Brand, and Sales for full-funnel alignment, without owning paid acquisition day-to-day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a strategic thought partner to Otter&#39;s leadership on growth strategy, PLG vs sales-assisted motions, and how to sequence product and partnership bets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in growth marketing, growth product, or product-led growth roles, with experience also leading product or partnership launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operator experience in a $50M+ ARR environment (SaaS, marketplace, or high-growth product company), ideally with SMB or operator-facing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional execution with engineering and product. You think in terms of product surfaces, not just campaigns, and you can write briefs engineers can build from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concrete track record of shipping growth experiments — activation lifts, conversion improvements, upsell motions — with results you can speak to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading at least one significant GTM launch (product or partnership) end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency. Comfortable in SQL, Mixpanel/Amplitude, and modern growth tooling. You can pull your own data and design your own tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product and commercial instincts. You&#39;re comfortable pushing back on Product about positioning and on BD about partnership terms when the math doesn&#39;t work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a high-growth, high-ambiguity environment where the scope of the role will shift across quarters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to influence and present to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience with PLG motions in SMB software, lifecycle marketing, or co-marketing with strategic partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
