&lt;li&gt;Work alongside with firmware and robotics engineers to ensure cohesive system functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects through rollout and production support, including testing, observability, incident diagnosis, and iterative improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a strong example through design reviews, code reviews, technical documentation, and thoughtful engineering tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, improve development practices, and help establish the technical culture and standards of the Los Angeles team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to hiring and technical calibration as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of strong software engineering experience, including ownership of complex systems or initiatives across multiple components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical design and execution in ambiguous, fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in at least one backend language; Go experience is valuable but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
