&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When another party is at fault for damage to an Atoms vehicle or a loss we’ve paid, those&amp;nbsp;dollars should come back to us. As Subrogation Specialist, you own that&amp;nbsp;recovery—identifying opportunities, building airtight files with our telematics and&amp;nbsp;dashcam evidence, and pursuing at-fault parties and their carriers. This is a role that&amp;nbsp;pays for itself: strong subrogation is a direct, measurable return to the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review new and open claims to identify subrogation and recovery potential, including deductible recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and document recovery files using police reports, Samsara telematics, dashcam footage, repair estimates, and driver statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursue at-fault third parties and their insurers; present demands, negotiate, and drive claims to recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inter-company arbitration (e.g., Arbitration Forums) filings and responses where negotiation stalls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply comparative/contributory negligence principles by jurisdiction to maximize net recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track recovery metrics—dollars identified, pursued, and collected—and report results to Risk leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Claims Coordinator, Claims Manager, and legal on litigated or high-value recoveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of auto subrogation experience (carrier, TPA, or fleet).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills and a track record of collected recoveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of comparative/contributory negligence and inter-company arbitration procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with auto physical-damage estimating and total-loss valuation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: adjuster license, arbitration experience, and comfort working from telematics/video evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recoverable dollars are consistently identified early—not missed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Net recovery dollars grow quarter over quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
