&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Hardware &amp;amp; Manufacturing TPM owns the queue where onsite hardware and QC issues meet engineering — the seam between the build floor (OEM production lines, upfit partners, kitting) and the teams that own the design. This role triages incoming hardware issues across active builds, on-road transport truck kitting and off-road mining kit installs alike, decides what escalates and to whom, and owns inventory issues before they hold up a build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today those reports land in a shared channel with no consistent triage, so a cosmetic issue and a line-stopping one compete for attention in whatever order they arrive. This role replaces that with a single owned queue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intake &amp;amp; Triage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a single intake queue for hardware and QC issues reported from build lines and field sites, replacing today&#39;s mix of ad hoc Slack messages and DMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage every incoming issue by severity and impact — distinguishing a line-stopping defect from a cosmetic one — rather than working items in the order they arrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and hold response-time expectations for build partners and plant contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dev-Queue Prioritization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize the engineering dev queue against what&#39;s actually blocking a build or a site, not against whichever issue was reported most recently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify when several individual tickets are the same underlying defect, and roll them into one engineering fix rather than let them get worked separately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onsite QC &amp;amp; Inventory Escalation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own escalation for onsite QC failures and inventory shortages — the shared point between the field/build floor and engineering, supply chain, and manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track recurring hardware defects (wrong part revisions, bracket or jig issues, harness defects) back to their root cause, and escalate to the owning team: engineering, supplier, or the line itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate hardware issues affecting truck builds across both on-road transport upfit lines and off-road mining kit installs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware, manufacturing, or field-ops background — has worked the floor, not just reviewed reports about it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable as the triage point between site or build partners and engineering: thick skin, high urgency, able to make a prioritization call with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has stood up an intake or QC process from scratch, not just operated one someone else built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record working with vehicle or heavy-equipment hardware (wiring harnesses, sensor/compute mounting, electromechanical assemblies).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with on-road commercial vehicle (Class 8 truck) upfit, kitting, or OEM production-line environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with off-road or heavy industrial equipment (mining, construction) hardware builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with supplier and inventory escalation, and part-revision control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linear or a similar ticketing tool for tracking build issues to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on real, production-deployed autonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technology that directly improves safety, efficiency, and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex challenges in demanding, real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a fast-moving team with high ownership and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See your work deployed and making a difference in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with experienced engineers and industry operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
