&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting AI/ML, software engineering, robotics, autonomy, or similarly specialized technical talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success finding and engaging passive candidates in highly competitive talent markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sourcing fundamentals and the ability to build a search rather than depend primarily on inbound applicants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar technical domains quickly and translate technical requirements into effective sourcing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand what candidates actually built, owned, and contributed to within complex technical organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with engineering leaders and senior hiring managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and willingness to challenge a search strategy when candidate or market evidence doesn&#39;t support it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple complex searches without sacrificing quality or candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and comfort operating in a fast-moving environment with evolving priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d especially like to meet you if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have recruited in areas such as foundation models, computer vision, perception, autonomous vehicles, robotics, multimodal AI, world models, reinforcement learning, ML systems, or ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to be an ML engineer. But you should be curious enough about the technology to learn the difference between someone who used a model, trained a model, built the systems around a model, and actually developed the model architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
