&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because Atoms employs its drivers and operations staff as W-2 team members, workers’&amp;nbsp;compensation is one of our most significant and people-critical exposures. As Workers’&amp;nbsp;Compensation Specialist, you will own our WC program end to end and across multiple&amp;nbsp;states—managing claims from first report through resolution, driving injured team&amp;nbsp;members back to health and work, and partnering with People, Safety, and Operations&amp;nbsp;to prevent injuries in the first place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of workers’ compensation claims across all Atoms markets, from first notice of injury through resolution and closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison to our TPA, carrier(s), and defense counsel; monitor adjuster performance, reserves, and claim strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and administer return-to-work and modified/light-duty programs in partnership with People and Operations to reduce lost time and indemnity cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate incident investigation with Safety, ensuring root-cause findings feed back into injury-prevention efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with multi-state workers’ compensation statutes and posting/reporting requirements (California and Texas in particular).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain OSHA 300/300A logs and support all regulatory recordkeeping and injury reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze claim trends, frequency/severity, and cost drivers; deliver regular reporting to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage medical provider networks and support timely, appropriate care for injured team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide loss and exposure data to support annual WC program renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on workers’ compensation claims experience, ideally multi-state; California WC experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of California and Texas workers’ compensation statutes, benefit structures, and dispute processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing TPAs, adjusters, and defense counsel, and holding them accountable to outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success building or running return-to-work / modified-duty programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization, written communication, and comfort with a fast-moving, high-volume environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: professional designation (e.g., WCCP, ARM, CPCU coursework), RMIS experience, and exposure to a distributed/multi-site workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Injured team members feel supported, informed, and return to work safely and promptly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lost-time claims and total WC cost trend down relative to headcount growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay fully compliant across every market it operates in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Atoms, you’ll work on one of the defining challenges of our time—bringing automation into the physical world to drive real, lasting impact. We exist to uncover valuable unknown truths and turn them into progress, which means constantly pushing beyond what’s known and building what doesn’t yet exist. The work is ambitious and often challenging, but it’s grounded in a shared sense of purpose and a team committed to seeing it through together. Our work only matters if it serves others, and we know that meaningful progress depends on the trust of the people we serve and the strength of our team—so we invest in both, creating an environment where you can do your best work and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
